---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';

const sections = [
  {
    heading: 'Who this is from',
    body: [
      `Decorna is built and run by <strong>Muhammad Asad</strong>. In this policy, "I" and "the app" mean Decorna and the person behind it.
       You can reach me at <a href="mailto:m.asad.chatthaa@gmail.com">m.asad.chatthaa@gmail.com</a>.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'What Decorna does with your data, feature by feature',
    body: [
      `<strong>Photos you take or choose.</strong> To redesign a space, the photo is sent over an encrypted connection to my server, then to an AI provider
       (Google Gemini or OpenAI) that returns the redesigned image. A short check, which confirms the photo matches the category you picked, works the same way.
       The photo is used only for that request. I do not keep your original photo on my servers, and I do not use your photos to train any model.
       The finished image waits in private storage only until your device confirms it has arrived, so a dropped connection does not cost you a credit; it is then deleted.`,
      `<strong>Your saved designs.</strong> Designs you save live on your device. They are not uploaded to my servers. Deleting the app, or choosing
       Profile, Reset All Saved Data, removes them.`,
      `<strong>Your account.</strong> You can use Decorna without one. If you sign in, with Apple or with an email address and a 6-digit code, I store your account id,
       your email address (Apple may give me a private relay address instead), your name and profile photo if you add them, your credit balance and plan, and any invite code you
       use or share. This is what lets your credits follow you to a new phone.`,
      `<strong>Without an account.</strong> A random identifier is kept in your device's Keychain. It counts your free credits so that reinstalling the app does not reset them.
       It is not linked to your name or contact details.`,
      `<strong>Purchases.</strong> Subscriptions and credit packs are sold and billed by Apple. I use RevenueCat to confirm what you own. I receive your purchase history and a user id,
       never your card or payment details.`,
      `<strong>Usage and crash data.</strong> I use PostHog to see which parts of the app are used and to receive crash reports. That includes taps and screens, your app version,
       device model, iOS version, language and plan, and your account id when you are signed in. It never includes your photos, your prompts, your email address or your name.`,
      `<strong>Notifications.</strong> Decorna asks before sending notifications. If you agree, your device's push token is stored with your account so I can send them,
       and removed when you sign out or delete the account. A notification that your redesign is ready is created on your device.`,
      `<strong>Email.</strong> I send the 6-digit codes you ask for, and a short welcome, password-changed or account-deleted message, through a mail service (Resend). I do not send marketing email.`,
      `<strong>If you write to me.</strong> The messages you send to support, and the app version and phone model in them, are used to answer you.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'What I do not do',
    body: [
      `I do not sell your data. I do not show ads. I do not track you across other companies' apps or websites. I do not build a profile of you for anyone else.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Who else handles data for me',
    body: [
      `These services process data only to run the parts of Decorna described above:
       Supabase (accounts, credits and the server that talks to the AI providers), Google Gemini and OpenAI (image generation), Apple (sign-in, purchases, notifications),
       RevenueCat (purchase status), PostHog (usage and crash data) and Resend (email). Each handles data under its own terms and privacy policy.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Keeping it and deleting it',
    body: [
      `Account data is kept while your account exists. <strong>To delete it, open Profile, Account, Delete Account.</strong> That removes your account, credits and the records linked to
       them from my servers. The deletion cannot be undone and cannot be requested twice for the same account.`,
      `You can also ask me to delete or export your data, or correct it, by emailing <a href="mailto:m.asad.chatthaa@gmail.com">m.asad.chatthaa@gmail.com</a> from the address on the account.
       Usage and crash data cannot be tied back to you after your account is deleted.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Permissions the app asks for',
    body: [
      `<strong>Camera</strong>, to photograph a room, exterior or garden. <strong>Photo library</strong>, to pick a photo and to save your redesign. <strong>Notifications</strong>, optional.
       You can change any of these in iOS Settings.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Children',
    body: [
      `Decorna is not directed at children under 13, and I do not knowingly collect their data. If you believe a child has sent me data, write to me and I will delete it.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Changes to this policy',
    body: [
      `If I change what the app collects, I will update this page and its date, and tell you in the app when the change matters. The date above is the version in force.`,
    ],
  },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Decorna Privacy Policy"
  description="What Decorna collects, why, who processes it, and how to delete it."
  path="/decorna/privacy/"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  meta="Last updated 11 October 2026"
  intro="Decorna redesigns a space from your photo. This page says exactly what that involves, in plain words."
  sections={sections}
/>
